<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL"
                  xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC"
                  xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:bootstrap.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/0.1.0/processes/ns#"
                  id="Definitions_MountSubgraph"
                  targetNamespace="https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/workflows">

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       Mount a declared subgraph — ONE process for every content source.

       The owner, 2026-10-03: "It's the same pattern. One of them is mounting
       the directory while one of them is mounting a branch. Another mount
       type could come in the future. A sub graph declares where it's getting
       its content." Bean l4ay.

       So there is no "mount a branch" process beside a "read a directory"
       one. Every step that reads or writes a declared subgraph starts here:
       resolve the source ONCE (declaration, then the instance config's
       override by id), then branch on its KIND. A kind this diagram has no
       flow for is refused rather than read as a directory.
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

  <bpmn:process id="Process_MountSubgraph" name="Mount a declared subgraph" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>Making a declared subgraph's content available at its declared path, whatever its content source.

You are in this process whenever a step is about to read or write the contents of a declared subgraph — beans, todos, fsh-guts, or any directory a declaration names. The source is resolved once, by `declaredSubgraph` (`schemas/harness-config.ts`) through `resolveSubgraphSource` (`schemas/subgraph-source.ts`): the instance config's `subgraphSources` override by id, then the entry's `source`, then a legacy `storage`, then the `directory` default.

The gateway is on the source KIND, and its flows are the only places the kinds differ. A `directory` subgraph is already where its path says, and writing it is an ordinary commit. A `branch` subgraph is mounted from the declared branch's tip into its path, and written back by splicing onto the tip without force. A kind with no flow here is refused.</bpmn:documentation>

    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_MountSubgraph">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_MountPipeline" name="Build pipeline">
        <bpmn:documentation>Mechanical: every decision on this lane is read off the resolved source, so the same declaration mounts the same way in every container, and an override in the instance config is the only thing that changes it.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:role ref="build-pipeline"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_SubgraphWanted</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_ResolveSource</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_SourceKind</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_UseCheckoutPath</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_MountBranchTip</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_RefuseUnknownKind</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_Join</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Mounted</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Refused</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>

    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_SubgraphWanted" name="A step needs a&#10;declared subgraph"/>

    <bpmn:task id="Task_ResolveSource" name="Resolve the subgraph's&#10;content source">
      <bpmn:documentation>
        `declaredSubgraph(start, id)`: the declaring instance, the entry, and the
        resolved source with `declaredIn` saying which layer answered. Never read
        `source` off the declaration directly — the config override and the
        legacy `storage` field are folded in by the resolver and nowhere else.
        A contradiction (both `source` and `storage`; a `qa` subgraph keyed by
        tip) throws here, before anything is mounted.
      </bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="directory-conventions"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_SourceKind" name="Which source kind?">
      <bpmn:documentation>The resolved source's `kind`: `directory`, `branch`, or a kind this diagram has no flow for.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>

    <bpmn:task id="Task_UseCheckoutPath" name="Use the checkout path&#10;in place">
      <bpmn:documentation>
        A `directory` source IS its declared path. Nothing is mounted; a write is
        an ordinary commit on the working branch, which is why `branch-store
        push` answers "commit through git" for it rather than pushing anything.
      </bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="directory-conventions"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:task id="Task_MountBranchTip" name="Mount the branch tip&#10;at the declared path">
      <bpmn:documentation>
        A `branch` source keyed by `tip`: `branch-store mount --id &lt;dir-id&gt;`
        writes the tip's files at the declared path, so every reader finds the
        directory where it always was; `push` splices edits back onto the tip,
        never forcing, and a same-file race is a conflict. The branch's NAME is
        the declaring directory's `storage` (or `source`) — a branch no
        declaration names is refused rather than guessed. A `commit`-keyed branch is read
        per commit through its own store (`qa-store`), not mounted.
      </bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="directory-conventions"/><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="content-context-and-state-graphs"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:task id="Task_RefuseUnknownKind" name="Refuse: no flow for&#10;this source kind">
      <bpmn:documentation>
        A kind added to the union (a graph database, say) before this diagram
        and the mount tool learn it. Refused with its own exit code — reading it
        as a directory would scan an empty path and report it clean, the `dh4f`
        defect.
      </bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="directory-conventions"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_Join"/>

    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Mounted" name="Subgraph content&#10;at its declared path"/>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Refused" name="Refused, with&#10;the reason"/>

    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_M1" sourceRef="Start_SubgraphWanted" targetRef="Task_ResolveSource"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_M2" sourceRef="Task_ResolveSource" targetRef="GW_SourceKind"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_M3" name="directory" sourceRef="GW_SourceKind" targetRef="Task_UseCheckoutPath"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_M4" name="branch" sourceRef="GW_SourceKind" targetRef="Task_MountBranchTip"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_M5" name="any other kind" sourceRef="GW_SourceKind" targetRef="Task_RefuseUnknownKind"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_M6" sourceRef="Task_UseCheckoutPath" targetRef="GW_Join"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_M7" sourceRef="Task_MountBranchTip" targetRef="GW_Join"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_M8" sourceRef="GW_Join" targetRef="End_Mounted"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_M9" sourceRef="Task_RefuseUnknownKind" targetRef="End_Refused"/>

  </bpmn:process>

  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="Diagram_MountSubgraph">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="Plane_MountSubgraph" bpmnElement="Process_MountSubgraph">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_Lane_MountPipeline" bpmnElement="Lane_MountPipeline" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="160" y="60" width="1080" height="360"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_Start_SubgraphWanted" bpmnElement="Start_SubgraphWanted">
        <dc:Bounds x="200" y="212" width="36" height="36"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_Task_ResolveSource" bpmnElement="Task_ResolveSource">
        <dc:Bounds x="280" y="190" width="160" height="80"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_GW_SourceKind" bpmnElement="GW_SourceKind" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="480" y="205" width="50" height="50"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_Task_UseCheckoutPath" bpmnElement="Task_UseCheckoutPath">
        <dc:Bounds x="580" y="90" width="170" height="70"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_Task_MountBranchTip" bpmnElement="Task_MountBranchTip">
        <dc:Bounds x="580" y="195" width="170" height="70"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_Task_RefuseUnknownKind" bpmnElement="Task_RefuseUnknownKind">
        <dc:Bounds x="580" y="310" width="170" height="70"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_GW_Join" bpmnElement="GW_Join" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="800" y="150" width="50" height="50"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_End_Mounted" bpmnElement="End_Mounted">
        <dc:Bounds x="920" y="157" width="36" height="36"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_End_Refused" bpmnElement="End_Refused">
        <dc:Bounds x="920" y="327" width="36" height="36"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="E_F_M1" bpmnElement="F_M1">
        <di:waypoint x="236" y="230"/><di:waypoint x="280" y="230"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="E_F_M2" bpmnElement="F_M2">
        <di:waypoint x="440" y="230"/><di:waypoint x="480" y="230"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="E_F_M3" bpmnElement="F_M3">
        <di:waypoint x="505" y="205"/><di:waypoint x="505" y="125"/><di:waypoint x="580" y="125"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="E_F_M4" bpmnElement="F_M4">
        <di:waypoint x="530" y="230"/><di:waypoint x="580" y="230"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="E_F_M5" bpmnElement="F_M5">
        <di:waypoint x="505" y="255"/><di:waypoint x="505" y="345"/><di:waypoint x="580" y="345"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="E_F_M6" bpmnElement="F_M6">
        <di:waypoint x="750" y="125"/><di:waypoint x="825" y="125"/><di:waypoint x="825" y="150"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="E_F_M7" bpmnElement="F_M7">
        <di:waypoint x="750" y="230"/><di:waypoint x="825" y="230"/><di:waypoint x="825" y="200"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="E_F_M8" bpmnElement="F_M8">
        <di:waypoint x="850" y="175"/><di:waypoint x="920" y="175"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="E_F_M9" bpmnElement="F_M9">
        <di:waypoint x="750" y="345"/><di:waypoint x="920" y="345"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
    </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
  </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
</bpmn:definitions>
